            <ArticleTitle>Arm pain and fever as an unusual presentation of lobar pneumonia in a 3-year-old girl: case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>420-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/PEC.0b013e318218754e</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Children with pneumonia presenting with extrathoracic pain, such as abdominal pain, have been previously described. In this report, we describe a 3-year-old girl with fever and right arm pain who was found to have an apical lobar pneumonia.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
